slides.content:
# `generateMetadata` Function

When metadata depends on fetched data or route params, use `generateMetadata`.

```jsx
// pages/posts/[id].js
export async function generateMetadata({ params }) {
  const post = await fetch(`https://.../posts/${params.id}`).then(r => r.json());
  return {
    title: post.title,
    description: post.excerpt,
  };
}
```

This runs on the server, so the metadata is injected into the final HTML.

slides.codeSnippet:
// pages/posts/[id].js
export async function generateMetadata({ params }) {
  const post = await fetch(`https://jsonplaceholder.typicode.com/posts/${params.id}`).then(r => r.json());
  return {
    title: post.title,
    description: post.body.slice(0, 150),
    openGraph: {
      images: [`/og-posts/${params.id}.jpg`],
    },
  };
}

export default function Post({ post }) { /* ... */ }

