# Setting Global Defaults

In your root layout (`app/layout.js` in App Router, or `_app.js` with Head in Pages Router), you can set a `metadataBase` and a `title` template.

```jsx
// In layout.js (App Router)
export const metadata = {
  title: {
    template: '%s | My Site',
    default: 'My Site',
  },
  description: 'Welcome to my site',
};
```

Then in child pages, just set `title: 'About'` and it becomes "About | My Site".
